WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.338 --> 00:00:01.386
(zooming)

00:00:01.386 --> 00:00:03.170
(boom)

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:04.510
- What's up Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:05.971
My one word is BelieveIn.

00:00:05.971 --> 00:00:08.452
I believe in people more than
they believe in themselves.

00:00:08.452 --> 00:00:09.851
And my sincere hope is that

00:00:09.851 --> 00:00:11.647
if you believe in yourself as much

00:00:11.647 --> 00:00:15.026
as I believe in you, you'll
be able to change the planet.

00:00:15.026 --> 00:00:16.354
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:16.354 --> 00:00:19.330
today we're going to learn
nine surprising facts

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.293
about Will Smith.

00:00:21.293 --> 00:00:24.293
(slow techno music)

00:00:31.992 --> 00:00:33.101
(ding)

00:00:33.101 --> 00:00:35.820
Fact number one, he believes
he can become president

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.443
of the United States if he wanted to.

00:00:38.443 --> 00:00:40.761
- A few months ago I
said that I believe that,

00:00:40.761 --> 00:00:43.460
(Jonathan laughs)
if I chose to,

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.765
I could be the president
of the United States.

00:00:46.765 --> 00:00:50.294
And I think, as I've had a
chance to intellectualize

00:00:50.294 --> 00:00:52.189
why I said that,
- Yeah.

00:00:52.189 --> 00:00:56.356
- and I think that there's
a certain delusional quality

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:02.191
that all successful people have to have.

00:01:03.723 --> 00:01:06.227
You have to believe
that something different

00:01:06.227 --> 00:01:10.839
than what has happened for
the last 50 million years

00:01:10.839 --> 00:01:12.925
- Yeah, yeah right.
- of history,

00:01:12.925 --> 00:01:16.319
you have to believe that
something different can happen.

00:01:16.319 --> 00:01:20.193
And I say it to my friends all the time

00:01:20.193 --> 00:01:21.971
and we laugh about it.

00:01:21.971 --> 00:01:26.054
I truly, honestly, as I
sit before you right now,

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:29.680
as honestly as I can say it to you,

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:31.017
I truly believe that I could

00:01:31.017 --> 00:01:33.094
be the president if I wanted to.

00:01:33.094 --> 00:01:35.453
And as bizarre as that may sound

00:01:35.453 --> 00:01:37.151
- Yeah.
- to people that

00:01:37.151 --> 00:01:39.157
have traveled the path before me,

00:01:39.157 --> 00:01:41.771
and to people who actually
know how difficult it is,

00:01:41.771 --> 00:01:44.596
foolish Will Smith honestly believes it.

00:01:44.596 --> 00:01:45.925
(ding)

00:01:45.925 --> 00:01:47.324
- Fact number two, he knows how

00:01:47.324 --> 00:01:50.953
to solve the Rubik's Cube really quickly.

00:01:50.953 --> 00:01:55.045
(Will muttering)
- [Woman] Two minutes.

00:01:55.045 --> 00:01:57.481
